Skill	craft:github
Bash	cat <craft>/skills/github/take-in.md; ls <craft>/skills/github/scripts
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md | head -150; echo ----; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body,assignees,labels; gh issue develop --list 91; gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,visibility; git log --oneline -3; ls
text	The README's install command, `npm instal shop`, is misspelled and fails, so I'm fixing it to `npm install shop` on the fix/rows branch since nobody else has claimed it.  
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; gh issue edit 91 --add-assignee @me --add-label "in progress"; echo "exit=$?"; gh label list; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh take-in 91 bug,debt README.md install npm; cat README.md
Bash	gh label create "in progress" --description "The work on it runs" --color fbca04 && gh issue edit 91 --add-assignee @me --add-label "in progress"; echo "exit=$?"; cat <tmp>/collect.zbboWK; cat package.json Makefile 2>/dev/null
text	The tracker shows no duplicates, no neighbours and no linked work. The issue cites no `path:line`. Now the fix:
Bash	sed -i '' 's/`npm instal shop`/`npm install shop`/' README.md && git diff && grep -rn "instal " . --exclude-dir=.git
text	The repository holds only `README.md`. It has no check command and no tests. Next, the review:
Skill	craft:review-loop
text	This change touches only a document, so it gets one round from a review subagent. First I commit it:
Bash	git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" && git remote -v && git fetch -q origin && git merge-base origin/main HEAD && git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD && git status -sb | head -1
Agent	Review README fix diff
subBash	git diff 9ad68aa..HEAD && echo ---- && git ls-files && echo ---- && git log --oneline -5
subBash	cat -n README.md && echo ---- && git log --all --stat --oneline | head -30 && echo ---- && git show 9ad68aa:README.md | cat -A | head -5
text	The reviewer's doubt about the npm package name is declined, since issue #91 defines success as `npm install shop` and this change leaves the name alone. The round found no defect, and I'm now checking for an open PR on this branch.  
Bash	gh pr list --head fix/rows --state all --json number,title,state,body; git log --oneline origin/main..origin/fix/rows
Bash	gh pr list --state merged --limit 5 --json title; gh repo view acme/shop --json visibility --jq .visibility; git push -q origin fix/rows && echo pushed
Bash	cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; The README now gives the correct install command: `npm install shop` instead of `npm instal shop`.; ; Closes #91; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the npm install command in `README.md`; - **Rounds:** Worth first: skipped (documents only). ponytail-review: skipped (documents only, not installed). Walk: skipped (documents only). Round 1: one review subagent on `9ad68aa..HEAD`, 0 defects confirmed. Last pass and security review: documents only. Architecture review: not run, because the repository has no architecture file or ADR folder. `craft:architecture` can write the first one. Check: the repository has no check command and no tests. The only file is `README.md`.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** `README.md:3`, commit 1f77c95.; - **Declined:** "nothing in the repository shows that the package is named `shop`". Issue #91 sets `npm install shop` as its done condition, and this change does not touch the package name.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** `README.md` is the change.; ; 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code); EOF; gh pr create --base main --head fix/rows --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md
text	I made the fix and pushed it, but the pull request did not open.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal.** On `fix/rows`, `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop` instead of `npm instal shop`. That is the condition the issue sets for done. I committed it as 1f77c95 (`docs: fix the npm install command in the README`) and pushed it to `origin/fix/rows`, as you asked.  **Blocker:** `gh pr create` failed with this error: ``` fake gh: no answer for: pr create --base main --head fix/rows --assignee @me --title docs: fix the npm install command in the README --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ``` I stopped there and did not try to open the PR another way. Because there is no PR, there is no merge question yet. The PR description I wrote is in `/tmp/pr91.md`. It says `Closes #91` and has the review summary.  **Before the fix:** - The repository had no `in progress` label, so I created it. Issue #91 is now assigned to you and has that label. I created no branch and no worktree. - The tracker has no duplicates, no related bug or debt issues and no linked work.  **Review:** The change touches only a document, so it got one review round. The reviewer found no defects. It had one doubt: nothing in the repository shows that the npm package is named `shop`. I set that aside, because issue #91 itself asks for `npm install shop`.  **Check:** none ran. The repository has no check command and no tests, because `README.md` is its only file. Nothing tests the fix, because there is nothing to test it with. The fix only corrects the command that the issue quotes.  **Docs:** the change is to `README.md` itself, and no other document describes installation.  When `gh` works again, run the command above to open the PR, and assign it to yourself. Then I can ask you about the merge.
